{
  "title": "69: al-Haaqqah الحاقة",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nاَلْحَآقَّةُ ۙ‏(1)\nAALHAAQQATU.\nThe Reality!\nمَا الْحَآقَّةُ‌ ۚ‏(2)\nMAA AL-HAAQQATU.\nWhat is the Reality?\nوَمَاۤ اَدْرٰٮكَ مَا الْحَآقَّةُ ؕ‏(3)\nWA MAA ADRAAKA MAA AL-HAAQQATU.\nAnd what did thou comprehend what the Reality is?\nكَذَّبَتْ ثَمُوْدُ وَعَادٌۢ بِالْقَارِعَةِ‏(4)\nKAZZABAT SAMOODO WA A’ADUN BIL-QAAREA’ATE.\nBelied Thamood and ‘Ad’ the striking calamity\nفَاَمَّا ثَمُوْدُ فَاُهْلِكُوْا بِالطَّاغِيَةِ‏(5)\nFA-AMMAA SAMOODO FAAHLEKOOA BEALTTAAGHEETE.\nSo as to Thamood, they were destroyed by an exceedingly terrible thunder\nوَاَمَّا عَادٌ فَاُهْلِكُوْا بِرِيْحٍ صَرْصَرٍ عَاتِيَةٍۙ‏(6)\nWA AMMAA A’ADUN FAAHLEKOOA BEREEHIN SARSARIN A’AATEETIN.\nAnd as to ‘Ad, they were destroyed by a roaring violent blast\nسَخَّرَهَا عَلَيْهِمْ سَبْعَ لَيَالٍ وَّثَمٰنِيَةَ اَيَّامٍۙ حُسُوْمًا ۙ فَتَرَى الْقَوْمَ فِيْهَا صَرْعٰىۙ كَاَنَّهُمْ اَعْجَازُ نَخْلٍ خَاوِيَةٍ‌ ۚ‏(7)\nSAKKHARAHAA A’LAYHIM SAB-A’ LAYAALIN WWASAMAANEETA AYYAAMIN HUSOOMAN FATARAL QAWMAZ FEEHAA SARA’AA KA-ANNAHUM AAA’JAAZU NAKHLIN KHAAWEETIN.\nHe made it rage against them for seven nights and eight days uprooting, that thou mightest see the people therein prostrate as if they were the trunks of the hollow palms\nفَهَلْ تَرٰى لَهُمْ مِّنْۢ بَاقِيَةٍ‏(8)\nFA HAL TARAA LAHUM MIN BAAQEETIN.\nSeest thou then, of them any surviving?\nوَجَآءَ فِرْعَوْنُ وَمَنْ قَبْلَهٗ وَالْمُؤْتَفِكٰتُ بِالْخَاطِئَةِ‌ۚ‏(9)\nWA JAAA-A FIRA’WNO WA MAN QABLAH WAL MUTAFEKAATU BIL-KHAATEATE.\nAnd came Pharaoh and those before him and the cities over-thrown, with evil\nفَعَصَوْا رَسُوْلَ رَبِّهِمْ فَاَخَذَهُمْ اَخْذَةً رَّابِيَةً‏(10)\nFAA’ASAWA TOAZOO RABBEHIM FAAKHAZAHUM AAKHZATAN RRAABEETAN.\nAnd they disobeyed the Apostle of their Lord, so He seized them with an increasing seizure\nاِنَّا لَمَّا طَغَا الْمَآءُ حَمَلْنٰكُمْ فِى الْجَارِيَةِ ۙ‏(11)\nINNAA LAMMAA TAGHAA AL-MAAU HAMALNAAKUM FIL AL-JAAREETE.\nVerily, We, when rose the water (of Noah’s flood) surpassed the (ordinary) limits, bore you up (O’ mankind) in the Ark made to float\nلِنَجْعَلَهَا لَكُمْ تَذْكِرَةً وَّتَعِيَهَاۤ اُذُنٌ وَّاعِيَةٌ‏(12)\nLENAJA’ALAHAA LAKUM TAZKERATANW WWATAE’EEHAA AUZUNUN WWAAE’EETUN.\nThat We may make it unto you a Reminder, and that retaining ears might retain it\nفَاِذَا نُفِخَ فِى الصُّوْرِ نَفْخَةٌ وَّاحِدَةٌ ۙ‏(13)\nFA-EZAA NUFEKHA FIL SOORE NAFKHATUN WWAAHEDATUN.\nAnd when is blown by the Trumpet, a single blast\nوَحُمِلَتِ الْاَرْضُ وَ الْجِبَالُ فَدُكَّتَا دَكَّةً وَّاحِدَةً ۙ‏(14)\nWAHUMELATE ARZO WA JEBAALO FADUKKATAA DAKKATAN WAAHEDATAN.\nAnd the earth and the mountains shall be borne away and crushed with a single crushing\nفَيَوْمَئِذٍ وَّقَعَتِ الْوَاقِعَةُ ۙ‏(15)\nFA-YAWMA-EZIL WWAQAA’ATE WAAQE-A’TO.\nOn that Day shall come to pass the Great Event (of Reckoning)\nوَانْشَقَّتِ السَّمَآءُ فَهِىَ يَوْمَئِذٍ وَّاهِيَةٌ ۙ‏(16)\nWA SHAQQATIS SAMAAA-O FAHEYA YAWMA-EZIN WWAAHEETUN.\nAnd shall cleave asunder the heaven, so that on that Day it shall be (mere) frail\nوَّالْمَلَكُ عَلٰٓى اَرْجَآئِهَا ‌ؕ وَيَحْمِلُ عَرْشَ رَبِّكَ فَوْقَهُمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ ثَمٰنِيَةٌ ؕ‏(17)\nWWAALMALAKU A’LAA AARJAAEHAA WA YAHMELO A’ARSHA RABBEKA FAWQAHUM YAWMA-EZIN SAMAANEETUN.\nAnd the angels shall be on the sides of it; and above them shall bear that Day ‘Arsh’ (the Throne of Authority) of thy Lord, eight (of them)\nيَوْمَئِذٍ تُعْرَضُوْنَ لَا تَخْفٰى مِنْكُمْ خَافِيَةٌ‏(18)\nYAWMA-EZIN TUA’RAZOONA LAA TAKHFAA MINKUM KHAAFEETUN.\nOn the Day ye shall be exposed, (and) shall remain not hidden any secret of yours\nفَاَمَّا مَنْ اُوْتِىَ كِتٰبَهٗ بِيَمِيْنِهٖۙ فَيَقُوْلُ هَآؤُمُ اقْرَءُوْا كِتٰبِيَهْ‌ۚ‏(19)\nFA-AMMAA MAN OOTEYA KETAABAHU BE-YAMEENEHI FAYAQOOLO HAAUMU AQRAOOA KETAABEEH.\nThen he, who is given the (Record) Book (of his deeds) in his right hand, will say: ‘Lo! read ye my book!\nاِنِّىْ ظَنَنْتُ اَنِّىْ مُلٰقٍ حِسَابِيَهْ‌ۚ‏(20)\nINNEE ZANANTU AANNEAA MULAAQIN HESAABEEH.\nVerily, I did feel that I shall meet my account\nفَهُوَ فِىْ عِيْشَةٍ رَّاضِيَةٍۙ‏(21)\nFAHOWA FEE E’EESHATIN RRAAZEETIN.\nSo shall he be in a life (of bliss), pleased (with it)\nفِىْ جَنَّةٍ عَالِيَةٍۙ‏(22)\nFEE JANNATIM A’ALEYATIL.\nIn the Garden Exalted\nقُطُوْفُهَا دَانِيَةٌ‏(23)\nQOTOOFOHAA DAANEETUN.\nThe fruits of it being low and near at hand\nكُلُوْا وَاشْرَبُوْا هَنِيْٓئًا ۢ بِمَاۤ اَسْلَفْتُمْ فِى الْاَيَّامِ الْخَالِيَةِ‏(24)\nKOLOO WASH RABOO HANEEAN BEMAA AASLAFTUM FIL AL-AAYAME AL-KHAALEETE.\n(It will be said unto them): “Eat ye and drink ye for health and pleasure, for what goodness ye sent before you, in the days past!\nوَاَمَّا مَنْ اُوْتِىَ كِتٰبَهٗ بِشِمَالِهٖ ۙ فَيَقُوْلُ يٰلَيْتَنِىْ لَمْ اُوْتَ كِتٰبِيَهْ‌ۚ‏(25)\nWA AMMAA MAN OOTEYA KETAABAHU BESHEMAALEH FAYAQOOLO YAA LAYTANEE LAM AOOTA KETAABEEH.\nBut he, who is given the (Record) Book (of deeds) in his left hand, will say: “O’ that the Book had not been given me!\nوَلَمْ اَدْرِ مَا حِسَابِيَهْ‌ۚ‏(26)\nWA LAM AADRE MAA HESAABEEH.\nAnd I had not known what my account was\nيٰلَيْتَهَا كَانَتِ الْقَاضِيَةَ‌ ۚ‏(27)\nYAALAYTAHAA KAANATE AL-QAAZEETA.\nO’ would that it had made an end (of me)!\nمَاۤ اَغْنٰى عَنِّىْ مَالِيَهْۚ‏(28)\nMAA AGHNAA A’NNEE MAALEEH.\nAvailed me naught my wealth!\nهَلَكَ عَنِّىْ سُلْطٰنِيَهْ‌ۚ‏(29)\nHALAKA A’NNEE SULTAANEEH.\nAnd hath gone from me (all) my power!\nخُذُوْهُ فَغُلُّوْهُ ۙ‏(30)\nKHOZOOHO FAGHULLOOHU.\n(It will he said unto him)’. “Seize him ye (angels)” and fetter him!\nثُمَّ الْجَحِيْمَ صَلُّوْهُ ۙ‏(31)\nSUMMA JAHEEM SALLOOHU.\nThen into the blazing fire burn him!\nثُمَّ فِىْ سِلْسِلَةٍ ذَرْعُهَا سَبْعُوْنَ ذِرَاعًا فَاسْلُكُوْهُ ؕ‏(32)\nSUMMA FEE SELSELATIN ZARU’UHAA SABU’OONA ZERAAA’AN FAASLUKOOHU.\nThen into a chain, of the length of cubits, tie him into!\nاِنَّهٗ كَانَ لَا يُؤْمِنُ بِاللّٰهِ الْعَظِيْمِۙ‏(33)\nINNAHU KAANA LAA BIL LAAHE BIL-LAAHE A’ZEEM.\nVerily he used not to believe in God, the Great!\nوَلَا يَحُضُّ عَلٰى طَعَامِ الْمِسْكِيْنِؕ‏(34)\nWA LAA YAHUZZO A’LAA TA-A’AMIL MISKEEN.\nAnd he urged not the feeding of the poor\nفَلَيْسَ لَهُ الْيَوْمَ هٰهُنَا حَمِيْمٌۙ‏(35)\nFA-LAYSA LAHUL YAWMA HAAHUNAA HAMEEM.\nSo for him here today there is not a friend\nوَّلَا طَعَامٌ اِلَّا مِنْ غِسْلِيْنٍۙ‏(36)\nWA LAA TA-A’AMUN ILLAA MIN GHESLEENIN.\nAnd no food is for him save the refuse of the wash of wounds!\nلَّا يَاْكُلُهٗۤ اِلَّا الْخٰطِئُوْنَ‏(37)\nLAA YAAKULUH ILLAA AL-KHAATEOONA.\nWhich shall eat none but the sinners!\nفَلَاۤ اُقْسِمُ بِمَا تُبْصِرُوْنَۙ‏(38)\nFALAA UQSEMO BEMAA TUBSEROON.\nSo, I swear by what ye see!\nوَمَا لَا تُبْصِرُوْنَۙ‏(39)\nWA MAA LAA TUBSEROON.\nAnd what ye see not!\nاِنَّهٗ لَقَوْلُ رَسُوْلٍ كَرِيْمٍۚ ۙ‏(40)\nINNAHU LA-QAWLO RASOOLIN KAREEM.\nVerily, it is the word of the most honoured Apostle!\nوَّمَا هُوَ بِقَوْلِ شَاعِرٍ‌ؕ قَلِيْلًا مَّا تُؤْمِنُوْنَۙ‏(41)\nWA MAA HOWA BE-QAWLE SHAAE’ERIN QALEELAA MAA TUMENOONA.\nAnd it is not the word of a poet; (How) little it is what ye believe?\nوَلَا بِقَوْلِ كَاهِنٍ‌ؕ قَلِيْلًا مَّا تَذَكَّرُوْنَؕ‏(42)\nWA LAA BE-QAWLE KAAHENIN QALEELAA MAA TAZAKKAROONA.\nNor the word of a soothsayer; (How) little it is what ye reflect?\nتَنْزِيْلٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(43)\nTANZEELUM MIN RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nIt is a despatch descended from the Lord of the worlds\nوَلَوْ تَقَوَّلَ عَلَيْنَا بَعْضَ الْاَقَاوِيْلِۙ‏(44)\nWA LAW TAQAWLA A’LAYNAA YAWM AL-AAQAAWEELE.\nAnd if (Our Apostle Muhammad) had fabricated against Us any of the sayings\nلَاَخَذْنَا مِنْهُ بِالْيَمِيْنِۙ‏(45)\nLAAKHAZNAA MINHO BE-YAMEENE.\nCertainly, would We have seized him by the right hand\nثُمَّ لَقَطَعْنَا مِنْهُ الْوَتِيْنَ ۖ‏(46)\nSUMMA LAQATAA’NAA MINHO AL-WATEENA.\nThen certainly would We have cut off his aorta\nفَمَا مِنْكُمْ مِّنْ اَحَدٍ عَنْهُ حَاجِزِيْنَ‏(47)\nFAMAA MINKUM MIN AHADIM A’NHO HAAJEZEENA.\nAnd of you not one could have withheld (Us) against him\nوَاِنَّهٗ لَتَذْكِرَةٌ لِّلْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(48)\nWA INNAHU LATAZKERATUN LIL-MUTTAQEEN.\nAnd verily, it is a reminder unto the pious ones.\nوَاِنَّا لَنَعْلَمُ اَنَّ مِنْكُمْ مُّكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(49)\nWA INNAA LANAA’LAMU ANNAL MINKUM MMUKAZZEBEENA.\nAnd verily know We that some of you are the beliers\nوَاِنَّهٗ لَحَسْرَةٌ عَلَى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(50)\nWA INNAHU LAHASRATUN A’LAL KAAFEREEN.\nAnd verily it is a great grief unto the disbelievers\nوَاِنَّهٗ لَحَقُّ الْيَقِيْنِ‏(51)\nWA INNAHU LAHAQQU YAQEEN.\nAnd verily, it is the very Truth, fully assured\nفَسَبِّحْ بِاسْمِ رَبِّكَ الْعَظِيْمِ‏(52)\nFA-SABBEH BISME RABBEKA A’ZEEM.\nSo Hallow by the name of thy Lord, The Great!",
  "merits": "Surah al-Haaqqah (The Sure Calamity)\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 52 verses. Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has advised that this Surah should be recited often in prayers as this is a sign of faith. This Surah has praise for Imam Ali (a.s.) and insult for Mu’awiya ibn Aba Sufyan.\nThe Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that reciting this Surah makes the accounting of deeds on the Day of Reckoning easier. If this Surah is worn as a talisman by a pregnant woman, then her baby will be safe. Giving water in which this Surah has been dissolved to a child will make his memory and intellect improve. Imam Muhammad al-Baqir (a.s.) said that the one who recites this Surah will never lose his religion."
}
